{
  "id": "context-reinstatement",
  "term": "context reinstatement",
  "definition": "Context reinstatement is the return of the same conditions present during learning when memory is later tested, such as the same place, color, odor, or other surrounding cues. In psychology, it refers to the finding that memory is often better when the test context matches the original study context.",
